  "2026-05-29T21:58:55.866Z",codex,"2026-05-29 test fix: npm test initially failed because test/smoke.test.ts imported optionString/optionEnabled/optionInt from dist/index.js, but index.ts did not export them. Updated index.ts to export the option reader helpers and tightened readStringOption to trim/ignore empty strings, matching the expected runtime behavior for pm CLI normalized kebab/camel flags."
  "2026-05-29T21:59:18.725Z",codex-audit,"2026-05-29 functional readiness audit: existing in_progress readiness item selected, no new task created. Commands: npm run check PASS; npm test FAIL during npm run build:test because test/smoke.test.ts imports optionString, optionEnabled, and optionInt from dist/index.js but those exports are absent; npm run pack:dry-run PASS, tarball dry run listed 9 files and package size 10.9 kB; npm run changelog:check PASS. Hands-on: loaded built dist/index.js with a fake pm SDK registration harness; jira sync missing env failed clearly with required JIRA_BASE_URL, JIRA_API_TOKEN, and JIRA_EMAIL message and no token material; mocked Jira HTTPS search with redacted fake credentials and dry-run status filter reduced two mock issues to one in_progress item, dryRun true, wrote nothing. Secret scan: current tracked high-signal token git grep no hits; README email-like references classified as placeholder/example domains; git history high-signal token scan no hits. Blocker: npm test failure above."
  "2026-05-29T22:00:43.021Z",codex-audit,"2026-05-29 follow-up after concurrent Jira helper export fix: I observed source and dist changes already present in the worktree and did not author or revert them. Reran npm test for pm-jira; current result PASS with 7 tests passed, including option helper and missing-credential cases. Earlier audit failure is superseded by this rerun, provided the concurrent source changes are kept."
  "2026-05-29T22:33:14.343Z",codex,"2026-05-29 release-readiness refresh: package manifest/lock now target @unbrained/pm-cli >=2026.5.29 / ^2026.5.29 and pm-changelog ^2026.5.29-2 where applicable. Verified npm run check, npm test, npm run pack:dry-run, npm run audit:prod, npm run changelog:full, npm run changelog:check, npm run release:check, and pm validate. High-confidence worktree/history secret scan recorded no credential-shaped token findings for active package code; nonzero scan rows were classified as placeholders or vendored historical test data where applicable. Logs: /tmp/pm-active-package-gates-20260529.tsv, /tmp/pm-active-changelog-20260529.tsv, /tmp/pm-active-release-check-20260529.tsv, /tmp/pm-active-validate-20260529.tsv, /tmp/pm-active-secret-scan-20260529.tsv."
